MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_001: What's the idea of asking me to come out here,\nDante? Hey...is that a chariot from the arena?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_002: Well spotted! I had hoped you could assist me with\nsome research.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_003: I want you to lift this chariot over your head.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_004: Huh? What for?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_005: I'm after authenticity in my work. I went to a lot of\ntrouble setting this up through the arena.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_006: You're uniquely muscular, and I want to see those\npectorals bulging as they drip with sweat.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_007: There's a tale of the demigod Arago hoisting the\nlovely Olivia in her chariot as they cross a mountain.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_008: I'd like a glimpse of what that might have looked like\nfor reference. There's something in it for you as well.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_009: Weird request, but sure, if you say so. I'll help\na sister out.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_010: Then get to it, Goliath! Show me power tested to\nits absolute limit!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_011: Hyup!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_012: Hm. Didn't see much...testing there.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_013: Yeah, that wasn't so tough. Probably coulda lifted\nthe horse with it, if we had one.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_014: What is the meaning of this, Goliath?! That was\nthe opposite of what I wanted!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_015: What's got you all riled? I picked it up just like\nyou asked.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_016: I wanted to see struggle! Sweat! Something to make\nthe audience empathize a little!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_017: Then you shoulda asked me to do something hard!\nBwahaha!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_018: Can't you at least act the part? Have your muscles\ntwitch as if straining under the weight?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_019: Alley oop! You mean, like this?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_020: Oh! Terrible. Just terrible. I pour all my savings\ninto procuring a chariot, and look what I get.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_021: All I wanted was a spectacle to wow the crowds.\nWas that too much to ask?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_022: What's your deal, lady? I did everything you said.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_C_023: Yeesh, story of my life.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_001: ♪Hmm hmm.♪ Oh? Who's that, perchance? Oh, it's\nonly Goliath. But whatever is he doing?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_002: Easy now... Easy... The whole family's almost across.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_003: That colossus of combat belies a spirit gentle enough\nto watch over a family of waterfowl!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_004: Excellent form, Goliath! Keep at it!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_005: Who's there?! Enough with the shouting, lady.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_006: You're gonna scare the birds.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_007: An audience has trouble relating to a hero who's\ntoo great—who stands too tall above them.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_008: When faced with such a towering figure, the only\nresponse they can muster is to tremble in awe.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_009: Is this still about the chariot thing?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_010: But the heroic can become humanized, and therefore\nrelatable again to the common man.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_011: What you're doing now breaks the barrier between\naudience and performer so they can empathize!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_012: This is all going way over my head. Dumb it down\na little for me?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_013: Showing the audience foibles such as these helps\nthem to empathize with you better.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_014: I'm not an actor. Although I do play to a crowd\nsometimes, I guess.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_015: You're saying if the fight fans saw me doing this,\nthey'd think of me different?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_016: Exactly! No need to be so furtive about it. Take the\nbirds under your wing with gusto!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_017: Who told you I was trying to be all secret? I wasn't,\nreally! But hey, hang on a sec.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_018: If anybody did see me doing this, they'd yell at me\nfor bullying the poor little things.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_019: 'Cause the way I look always makes people think\nI'm the bad guy.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_020: Ah! The worry lines crisscrossing your brow!\nNow that's a face I've not seen in the arena.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_021: What a gift this is! Turn toward me, that I may drink\nin your torment and angst!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_B_022: Wh-what's with you, lady?! Get outta my face!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_001: Ho there, Goliath. You're looking well today.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_002: You again. What now, huh?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_003: Worry not. I wanted you to know that because of\nyou, I've gone back to the basics of dramaturgy.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_004: And I thought thanks were in order. I hope you'll\ncontinue to serve as my large, beefy muse.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_005: Uh. Sure! You want me to keep going, huh?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_006: Well, then there's something I gotta get off my chest\nwith you too.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_007: You said before how I don't gotta keep it a secret\nthat I look after the birds.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_008: So I stopped hiding it.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_009: And wouldn't you know, people started saying nicer\nstuff about me.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_010: Like, "So that guy wasn't watching the birds hoping\nto catch one for a snack?"
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_011: Ohoho! A snack! What a knee-slapper.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_012: Hey, it wasn't a joke! Damn, now I got a real good\nidea of what people think of me.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_013: On the other hand, things are easier now that I don't\nneed to sneak around. So, uh...thanks...
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_014: Interesting. Tell me, what's changed to make you\nso flustered?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_015: Whaddaya mean? I'm not nervous! You're nervous!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_016: No, no, I know that look when I see it, and I've never\nseen it in you. Something must have happened.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_017: For posterity, then, I must know what has drawn\nout this new and sheepish side of you!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_018: Back off! It was just, what do you call it...when you\ngot all up in my face last time.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_019: I thought "this lady's hair sure is messy, but she's\nnice-looking all the same." And then I felt weird.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_020: Oh, er... That's quite gracious of you.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_021: And you claimed you weren't an actor! Well, you\ncertainly stirred my empathy just now.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_022: You used that word before. What's it mean?\nWhen someone starts to like someone... Or...
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_023: Stop there! You're defining that all wrong!\nAnd do not confuse fiction and reality.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_024: Bwahahaha! It's pretty funny seeing you all panicked.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_025: You always act so high-and-mighty that it feels good\nfor you to get taken down a peg.
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_026: That devilish smile... Aaah! I must find an outlet\nfor these feelings, or I fear I shall burst!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_027: Uh, Dante? Whatcha doing down there?
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_028: Can't you see I'm writing?! With neither paper\nnor ink, the dirt itself must be my medium!
MID_SE_Gol_Dan_A_029: Ugh. So you always gotta write wherever you go?\nThat ain't a job—that's a curse.